      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11509624::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "Untreated conventional TC4 has a standard microstructure with moderate hardness and wear resistance.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Laser cladding a titanium-aluminum-carbon precursor promotes rapid solidification.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Ti-Al-C precursor reacts during cladding to form TiC particles in a TiAl matrix.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11509624::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hardness and wear improvements should hold in room-temperature tribological tests at moderate loads such as 10 N.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Ball-on-disk and oscillating tests are applicable methods for evaluating wear behavior.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7513041::web::014::3_4_hardness_and_wear_behaviour"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The coating will develop a fine-grained TiAl matrix containing uniformly dispersed hard TiC precipitates.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11509624::web::003::1_introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "yes"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiC particles strengthen the coating by obstructing dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "TiC particles pin grain boundaries.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A refined dual-phase matrix resists plastic deformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Strengthening and reduced plastic deformation increase hardness and wear resistance.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC11509624::web::003::1_introduction",
        "PMC7513041::web::014::3_4_hardness_and_wear_behaviour"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The cladded surface should be roughly 30–50% harder than untreated TC4.",
